        "crowdsourced_ai_results": [
          {
            "analysis": "This binary is a variant of the Mozi botnet, specifically targeting MIPS-based IoT devices. It exhibits worm-like propagation behaviors, utilizing a wide array of hardcoded exploits for GPON routers, Huawei Home Gateways, and Realtek SDK-based devices (Boaform exploits). Concrete malicious behaviors include device hardening by killing competing processes (telnetd, sshd, scfgmgr) and using iptables to block management ports (22, 23, 2323, 7547). It ensures persistence by modifying system initialization scripts such as /etc/rc.local and creating /etc/init.d/S95baby.sh. The binary also performs environment discovery via /proc/net/route and external IP identification through ipinfo.io. Relevant IOCs include the 'Mozi' file naming convention (e.g., Mozi.m, Mozi.a), the 'botv2' string, and exploit paths like /GponForm/diag_Form and /boaform/admin/formPing.",
